      "message": "Could we invert this logic?  It seems like it would be simpler to read if it were:\n\nif (mState !\u003d BluetoothAdapter.STATE_OFF\n\n        \u0026\u0026 mWaitForEnableRetry \u003c MAX_WAIT_FOR_ENABLE_DISABLE_RETRIES) {\n    mWaitForEnableRetry++;\n    Message enableDelayedMsg \u003d\n            mHandler.obtainMessage(MESSAGE_HANDLE_ENABLE_DELAYED);\n    mHandler.sendMessageDelayed(enableDelayedMsg, ENABLE_DISABLE_DELAY_MS);\n    break;\n}\nif (mWaitForEnableRetry \u003e\u003d MAX_WAIT_FOR_ENABLE_DISABLE_RETRIES) {\n\n    Slog.e(TAG, \"Timed out waiting for STATE_OFF\");\n}\nmWaitForEnableRetry \u003d 0;\nMessage restartMsg \u003d\n\n        mHandler.obtainMessage(MESSAGE_RESTART_BLUETOOTH_SERVICE);\nmHandler.sendMessageDelayed(restartMsg, getServiceRestartMs());\nSlog.d(TAG, \"Handle enable is finished\");\nbreak;",
